where the qubit index $j$ runs up the page, and time runs from left to right. 
This circuit has linear depth in the number of qubits it is applied to (and there is an ambiguity in the presence of periodic boundary conditions). 
However, it is simple to implement this operator via a constant-depth local unitary circuit followed by measurements and the application of a Pauli-$Z$ feed-forward operator. 
This is based on a simple gadget 
\begin{align}
