Within this subsection we present the results of simulating distributed memory and lattice surgery in the triangular color code, focusing on context-aware fault-improvement.
The color code is not matchable, and Tesseract is commonly used for its decoding already in the monolithic setting. In the distributed setting we use it to perform integrated decoding, again with the {short-beam} configuration.

